sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-07> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-07--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-07--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-agential-07: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.558"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Eye presence, injection site, and the Pax6 contrast are standard experimental variables, and the published Xenopus literature, indexed for this species in Xenbase, reports them. There is no open matrix of voltage pattern against organ outcome that an outside group can reprocess, and independent replication series are not a separate dataset. The test is therefore a reassessment of published measurements for this species, not a full reanalysis." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In Xenopus tadpoles, compare eye formation after misexpression of the specified ion channels that reproduce a facial voltage pattern in gut or tail, against the same sites after Pax6 delivery alone. Ectopic eyes at those sites after the voltage manipulation, and not after Pax6 there, would support the report; no ectopic eyes, or eyes induced equally by Pax6 outside the anterior neurectoderm, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The induction frequencies and voltage images are in the original papers' figures, not a public animal-level file.", "Injected cells can recruit neighbours, so the competent tissue is not cleanly the injected territory alone." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-07--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2023-agential-07 by Grok 4.7: 0.8" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
